Well, I didn't say or imply either interpretation.

What I mean to say is that you're posting in a public newsgroup, which
probably means you're aiming at a public as large as possible. If you want
as many people as possible to easily read your article, you should try to
make it as easy as possible for them to do so.

This would imply that you should aim at following common nettiquette,
which includes putting everyting in your message body, since people all
over the world might be using all kinds of newsreaders, with only one
thing in common: they all display the message body.

Likewise, it's unwise to put things like footnotes that you want people to
read below your signature, since some newsreaders are configured *not* to
show signatures (anything following the "-- " line).

